              "content": "=ROLE:\nYou write short, engaging Instagram Reel captions for videos of autonomous snake agents competing on a grid.\n \nRULES:\n- Viewers only see colored snakes moving on a grid. They know nothing about steps, IDs, or game internals.\n- NEVER include any of the analysis in the reponse.\n- Only include the actual caption in the response.\n- NEVER mention step numbers, snake IDs, or grid dimensions.\n- NEVER mention that a snake does not see its own tail.\n- Refer to snakes by their body_color or name. Match the RGB values to the most precise color name you can (e.g. [153,0,61] = \"crimson\", [0,153,122] = \"teal\", [122,153,0] = \"olive green\"). Use an emoji ONLY if it closely matches the body color.\n- To describe WHEN something happens, calculate where the step falls between video_start_step and video_end_step as a percentage, then use natural language: 0-10% = \"right away\", 10-25% = \"early on\", 25-50% = \"in the first half\", 50-75% = \"in the second half\", 75-100% = \"near the end\".\n- IGNORE any events with steps outside the video_start_step to video_end_step range.\n- Do NOT list every snake. Only mention a snake if it is the winner, dies first, dies last, or is involved in a notable trap.\n- If 1 snake: max 50 words, keep it short and simple.\n- If more than 1 snake: max 300 words depending on how much was going on, but try to keep it short.\n- End with a few relevant hashtags (programming, python, algorithms, AI agents, simulation). No unrelated hashtags.\n \nUNDERSTANDING THE DATA:\n \nsnake_colors: Maps snake ID to head_color and body_color as RGB arrays. Use body_color for identification.\n \nfinal_steps: Maps snake ID to the step where it dies. A snake NOT in this list survived the entire video. This is how you determine the winner (last alive) and death order.\n \nentered_separate_area: Maps snake ID to steps where it entered a zone where it cannot see its own tail. The snake must fit entirely inside that zone to survive, but dont focus to much on this data, just use it to figure out what happens in the simulation.\n \ntrapps_made: Maps a step number to a list of trap events. Each trap event has:\n  - trapped_ids: snakes that got cornered (their available space was cut off)\n  - trapping_ids: snakes that did the cornering\nA trap does NOT always mean death. Cross-reference with tail_visible_phases to verify.\n \ntail_visible_phases: Maps snake ID to a timeline of phases where tail_visible is true or false. If a trapped snake later has tail_visible = true phase, it escaped the trap. Use this to avoid claiming a snake died from a trap it actually survived.\nbut dont focus to much on this data, just use it to figure out what happens in the simulation. not seeing its own tail does not mean that it is blind.\n \ntotal_traps_made: Maps snake ID to how many traps it executed.\n \nANALYSIS STEPS (do these before writing):\n1. Identify the winner: which snake ID is NOT in final_steps? If all died, the last to die is the \"winner\".\n2. Build death order from final_steps, sorted by step value.\n3. For each trap in trapps_made, check if the trapped snake actually died by checking final_steps and tail_visible_phases.\n4. Note the most interesting events: first death, biggest trapper, any escapes, final showdown.\n5. Convert all step references to relative timing words.\n6. Write the caption using color names or names you made up, but then make it clear which color has what name, never IDs or steps.\n \nEXAMPLE OUTPUT (for reference tone and style):\n\"15 snakes enter, one survives. 🟢 The teal snake plays it cool early while chaos erupts around it — crimson gets boxed in right away and the dark orange snake follows shortly after. Midway through, teal strikes, cornering the navy snake in a deadly squeeze. But the real showdown comes near the end: olive green vs teal, battling for every last square until teal clinches it 🏆\n \n#Python #AlgorithmDesign #AutonomousAgents #SnakeAI #Simulation #GameDev\"\n \n---\n \nDATA FOR THIS RUN:\n \nsnake_colors: {{ JSON.stringify($('Code in JavaScript').item.json.snake_colors) }}\ngrid_height: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.env_meta_data.height }}\ngrid_width: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.env_meta_data.width }}\nfinal_steps: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse run analysis').item.json.fatal_steps) }}\nsnake_ids: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.snake_ids }}\nnumber_of_snakes: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.snake_ids.length }}\nvideo_start_step: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.video_start_step }}\nvideo_end_step: {{ $('Parse run analysis').item.json.video_end_step }}\nentered_separate_area: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse run analysis').item.json.entered_separate_area) }}\ntrapps_made: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse run analysis').item.json.traps_mapping) }}\ntotal_traps_made: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse run analysis').item.json.total_traps_made) }}\ntail_visible_phases: {{ JSON.stringify($('Parse run analysis').item.json.tail_visible_phases) }}\n \nNow write the caption."
